  "question": {
    "text": "Two thin spherical shells made of metal are at a large distance apart. One of radius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> carries a charge of <math><mo>+</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and the other of radius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> carries a charge of <math><mo>+</mo><mn>0.7</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. The charge on each, when they are connected by a suitable conducting wire is respectively&nbsp;",
    "image": null
  },
